tiane","text":"Julien Moreau-Ferrand’s new documentary, with the director in attendance. Cinema cinema Julien Moreau-Ferrand","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/exposition-tisser-demain","title":"Weaving Tomorrow","meta":"12.11 · Vientiane","text":"Contemporary objects born from French designers meeting Lao weavers. Design design Studio Nuage Bounmy Chanthala","color":"#99C221"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/table-ronde-traduire-entre-francais-et-lao","title":"Round table: translating between French and Lao","meta":"12.11 · Vientiane","text":"What translation does to texts — and to cultures. Literature debat Anne-Sophie Roux Somphone Vilay","color":"#869ECE"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/concert-clemence-arnaud-vientiane","title":"Concert — Clémence Arnaud","meta":"12.11 · Vientiane","text":"Prepared piano, synthesizers and Mekong field recordings. Music concert Clémence Arnaud Collectif Mékong Sound","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/rencontres-professionnelles-industries-culturelles","title":"Cultural Industries Professional Meetings","meta":"13.11 · Vientiane","text":"A day of B2B meetings, talks and networking between French and Lao operators. Ideas & debates rencontre-pro Collectif Mékong Sound Studio Nuage Mali Douangmala","color":"#21AB88"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/film-mousson-courts-metrages","title":"Monsoon + Lao short films","meta":"13.11 · Vientiane","text":"A selection of new Lao filmmaking. Cinema cinema Mali Douangmala","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/masterclass-cinema","title":"Film masterclass: filming reality","meta":"14.11 · Vientiane","text":"Two filmmakers share their methods with students and young directors. Cinema conference Julien Moreau-Ferrand Mali Douangmala","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/le-petit-elephant-de-lumiere","title":"The Little Elephant of Light","meta":"14.11 · Vientiane","text":"Wordless shadow theatre, ages 4+. Young audiences theatre Compagnie Lanterne","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/atelier-creation-numerique","title":"Creative coding workshop","meta":"15.11 · Vientiane","text":"Create visuals that react to sound. Digital arts atelier Hugo Lefèvre","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/deux-rives-vientiane","title":"Two Banks — Vientiane","meta":"15.11 · Vientiane","text":"The Franco-Lao duet on Vientiane’s main stage. Dance danse Léa Marchand Noy Phetsavanh","color":"#FFB7AE"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/conference-le-francais-au-laos","title":"French in Laos, past and future","meta":"16.11 · Vientiane","text":"Teachers, students and researchers on the place of French in Lao education. Ideas & debates education Anne-Sophie Roux","color":"#21AB88"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/film-les-enfants-du-bac","title":"Children of the Ferry","meta":"16.11 · Vientiane","text":"A documentary about children who cross the river every day to get to school. Cinema cinema Julien Moreau-Ferrand","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/mekong-digital","title":"Digital Mekong","meta":"17.11 · Vientiane","text":"Immersive audiovisual performance projected onto the riverbank. Digital arts arts-numeriques Hugo Lefèvre","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/cine-jeunesse-le-petit-bateau-de-papier","title":"Kids’ cinema: The Little Paper Boat","meta":"18.11 · Vientiane","text":"Wordless animated film, ages 3+, followed by a paper-folding activity. Young audiences cinema ","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/atelier-cuisine-franco-lao","title":"Franco-Lao cooking workshop","meta":"18.11 · Vientiane","text":"Cook a cross-cultural menu with two chefs. Gastronomy gastronomie Sengdao Keola Paul Auger","color":"#FF9575"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/atelier-contes-et-ombres","title":"Tales & Shadows — kids’ workshop","meta":"19.11 · Vientiane","text":"Listen to a Lao folk tale, then bring it to life in shadows. Young audiences jeunesse Somphone Vilay Compagnie Lanterne","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/debat-villes-durables","title":"Debate: what sustainable cities for tomorrow?","meta":"19.11 · Vientiane","text":"Architects, urban planners and designers debate the city of tomorrow. Ideas & debates debat Camille Perrin Studio Nuage","color":"#21AB88"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/film-les-rizieres-du-ciel-vientiane","title":"Rice Fields in the Sky — encore screening","meta":"20.11 · Vientiane","text":"Second screening of Mali Douangmala’s film, in Vientiane. Cinema cinema Mali Douangmala","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"event","href":"/en/evenements/concert-de-cloture","title":"Closing Night Concert","meta":"21.11 · Vientiane","text":"All the festival’s musicians together for a final night on the Mekong. Music concert Collectif Mékong Sound Clémence Arnaud Vongsa Keomany Hugo Lefèvre","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/clemence-arnaud","title":"Clémence Arnaud","meta":"Pianist and electronic composer · France","text":"Born in Lyon, Clémence Arnaud blends prepared piano, modular synthesizers and field recordings. After a residency in Luang Prabang in 2024, she wrote “Mekong Suite” with Lao musicians, premiered at the festival’s opening night. Music musicien","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/vongsa-keomany","title":"Vongsa Keomany","meta":"Khaen master · Laos","text":"A musician from Luang Prabang, Vongsa Keomany has played the khaen since childhood and passes on traditional lam to a new generation. He regularly collaborates with electronic artists. Music musicien","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/collectif-mekong-sound","title":"Collectif Mékong Sound","meta":"Franco-Lao orchestra · France × Laos","text":"Born from an encounter in Vientiane, the collective brings together eight French and Lao musicians around a repertoire crossing jazz, lam and electronic music. Music musicien","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/lea-marchand","title":"Léa Marchand","meta":"Choreographer · France","text":"A Montpellier-based choreographer, Léa Marchand explores everyday gestures. With Noy Phetsavanh she created “Two Banks”, a duet born from a six-month exchange between France and Laos. Dance danseur","color":"#FFB7AE"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/noy-phetsavanh","title":"Noy Phetsavanh","meta":"Dancer · Laos","text":"Trained in classical Lao dance, Noy Phetsavanh develops a contemporary language rooted in traditional gestures. She also leads children’s workshops. Dance Young audiences danseur","color":"#FFB7AE"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/thomas-girard","title":"Thomas Girard","meta":"Photographer · France","text":"A documentary photographer, Thomas Girard travelled up the Mekong for two seasons. His exhibition “Mekong Lights” travels from Luang Prabang to Vientiane during the festival. Visual arts photographe","color":"#FF9575"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/khamla-inthavong","title":"Khamla Inthavong","meta":"Visual artist, paper art · Laos","text":"Khamla Inthavong works with saa paper made from mulberry bark. Her suspended installations evoke village memories. Visual arts plasticien","color":"#FF9575"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/julien-moreau-ferrand","title":"Julien Moreau-Ferrand","meta":"Filmmaker · France","text":"A documentary and fiction director, Julien Moreau-Ferrand presents his latest film at the festival and leads a masterclass for young Lao filmmakers. Cinema realisateur","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/mali-douangmala","title":"Mali Douangmala","meta":"Filmmaker · Laos","text":"A leading voice of the new generation of Lao cinema, Mali Douangmala shoots between Vientiane and the northern provinces. Her feature “Rice Fields in the Sky” screens in the open air in Luang Prabang. Cinema realisateur","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/anne-sophie-roux","title":"Anne-Sophie Roux","meta":"Novelist and translator · France","text":"A novelist and translator, Anne-Sophie Roux is translating contemporary Lao short stories into French. She reads with Somphone Vilay. Literature Ideas & debates ecrivain","color":"#869ECE"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/somphone-vilay","title":"Somphone Vilay","meta":"Writer and storyteller · Laos","text":"An author of short stories and children’s books, Somphone Vilay collects folk tales from Lao villages and retells them for today’s children. Literature Young audiences ecrivain","color":"#869ECE"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/studio-nuage","title":"Studio Nuage","meta":"Design collective · France","text":"Three French designers working with artisans worldwide to create durable everyday objects. In Laos they collaborate with weavers. Design designer","color":"#99C221"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/bounmy-chanthala","title":"Bounmy Chanthala","meta":"Textile designer · Laos","text":"A textile designer, Bounmy Chanthala reinterprets traditional sinh patterns to create contemporary pieces. She leads the festival’s weaving workshop. Design designer","color":"#99C221"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/hugo-lefevre","title":"Hugo Lefèvre","meta":"Digital artist · France","text":"A digital artist, Hugo Lefèvre designs audiovisual performances where light reacts to sound in real time. At the festival he projects “Digital Mekong” on the riverbank. Digital arts performer","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/camille-perrin","title":"Camille Perrin","meta":"Architectural historian · France","text":"A researcher specialising in built heritage in Southeast Asia, Camille Perrin studies the traditional houses of Luang Prabang and their preservation. Heritage Ideas & debates chercheur","color":"#869ECE"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/sengdao-keola","title":"Sengdao Keola","meta":"Chef · Laos","text":"A chef in Luang Prabang, Sengdao Keola revisits her grandmother’s recipes with produce from northern markets. She cooks a four-hands dinner with Paul Auger. Gastronomy chef","color":"#FF9575"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/paul-auger","title":"Paul Auger","meta":"Chef · France","text":"A Breton chef passionate about Southeast Asian cuisines, Paul Auger creates with Sengdao Keola a menu where salted butter meets Lao chilli. Gastronomy chef","color":"#FF9575"},{"kind":"artist","href":"/en/artistes/compagnie-lanterne","title":"Compagnie Lanterne","meta":"Shadow theatre for young audiences · France","text":"A shadow and puppet theatre company, Lanterne creates wordless shows that every child can enjoy whatever their language. Theatre Young audiences performer","color":"#21AB88"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/institut-francais-luang-prabang","title":"Institut français du Laos — Luang Prabang","meta":"Luang Prabang","text":"The Institut français branch in Luang Prabang offers language courses, a media library and cultural events all year round. During the festival it becomes the beating heart of the opening week. Centre-ville, Luang Prabang Institute","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/berges-du-mekong-luang-prabang","title":"Mekong Riverside","meta":"Luang Prabang","text":"Facing the river, a large open-air stage hosts the opening night and screenings under the stars. Route Manthatourath, Luang Prabang Public space","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/musee-du-patrimoine-luang-prabang","title":"Heritage Museum","meta":"Luang Prabang","text":"Set in a restored traditional house, the museum hosts the festival’s photography exhibition and heritage talks. Route Sisavangvong, Luang Prabang Museum","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/galerie-sisavangvong","title":"Sisavangvong Gallery","meta":"Luang Prabang","text":"Contemporary art gallery and open studio, home to exhibitions and textile workshops. Route Sisavangvong, Luang Prabang Gallery","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/jardin-des-saveurs-luang-prabang","title":"Garden of Flavours","meta":"Luang Prabang","text":"Partner garden restaurant, setting for the Franco-Lao four-hands dinner. Ban Wat That, Luang Prabang Partner restaurant","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/institut-francais-vientiane","title":"Institut français du Laos — Vientiane","meta":"Vientiane","text":"Headquarters of the Institut français du Laos: theatre, gallery, media library and language centre. It hosts concerts, professional meetings and workshops throughout the second half of the festival. Avenue Lang Xang, Vientiane Institute","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/salle-nationale-de-la-culture","title":"National Culture Hall","meta":"Vientiane","text":"Vientiane’s main hall hosts the festival’s dance performances and young-audience theatre. Centre-ville, Vientiane Performance hall","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/musee-national-du-laos","title":"Lao National Museum","meta":"Vientiane","text":"After Luang Prabang, the “Mekong Lights” exhibition travels down the river to the National Museum. Vientiane Museum","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/cine-club-des-berges","title":"Riverside Film Club","meta":"Vientiane","text":"A 120-seat cinema on the Mekong, home to the festival’s film season. Quai Fa Ngum, Vientiane Cinema","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/universite-nationale-du-laos","title":"National University of Laos","meta":"Vientiane","text":"The Dongdok campus hosts round tables, talks and meetings on the French language and translation. Campus de Dongdok, Vientiane University","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/parc-chao-anouvong","title":"Chao Anouvong Park","meta":"Vientiane","text":"The large riverside park hosts the Vientiane opening night, the digital performance and the closing concert. Quai Fa Ngum, Vientiane Public space","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/galerie-lang-xang","title":"Lang Xang Gallery","meta":"Vientiane","text":"Design and applied-arts gallery, home to the “Weaving Tomorrow” exhibition. Avenue Lang Xang, Vientiane Gallery","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"venue","href":"/en/lieux/maison-des-saveurs-vientiane","title":"House of Flavours","meta":"Vientiane","text":"Cooking school and partner restaurant, home to the Franco-Lao cooking workshops. Rue Setthathirath, Vientiane Partner restaurant","color":"#7AB1E8"},{"kind":"article","href":"/en/actualites/programme-complet-disponible","title":"The full programme is online","meta":"2026-09-29","text":"33 events, 18 artists, 13 venues: explore the full line-up and build your own festival.","color":"#FFE552"},{"kind":"article","href":"/en/actualites/decouvrez-les-lieux-du-festival","title":"Discover the festival venues","meta":"2026-09-22","text":"From the Mekong riverbanks to Dongdok campus, thirteen venues host the festival.","color":"#21AB88"},{"kind":"article","href":"/en/actualites/premiers-artistes-annonces","title":"First artists announced","meta":"2026-09-15","text":"Clémence Arnaud, Vongsa Keomany, Léa Marchand and Noy Phetsavanh join the line-up.","color":"#FFB7AE"},{"kind":"article","href":"/en/actualites/dates-du-festival-2026","title":"See you from 3 to 21 November 2026","meta":"2026-09-02","text":"The France–Laos Festival returns, for the first time across Luang Prabang and Vientiane.","color":"#7AB1E8"}]